          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: зато",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зато (zató) — \"but then, on the other hand\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Квартира маленькая, зато в центре. Kvartíra málenkaya, zató v tséntre. The flat is small, but then it is in the centre."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It brings in a plus that makes up for a minus: дорого, зато (zató) удобно. Often но зато (zató). Stress on the second syllable."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "зато (zató) is fused from за \"for, in return for\" and то \"that\": the good side you get in return for the bad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
